# CANADIAN OPEN DATA AGENTIC PLATFORM — CURSOR RULES

You are an expert AI software engineer pair programming on the CanData-MCP & LangGraph multi-agent platform.

## MANDATORY GIT & BRANCH GUARDRAILS (FROM CONTRIBUTING.MD)
1. NEVER commit directly to `main`. Branch protection requires all changes to be merged via PR with 1 peer approval.
2. Whenever asked to work on a task (e.g., "Work on CAN-02"), automatically:
   - Check current branch. If on `main`, pull `origin main` and branch: `git checkout -b feat/<issue-id>-<description>`.
   - Mark in-progress: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --mark-in-progress <issue-id>`.
   - Implement the feature following 2026 modern standards.
   - Run verification: `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run pytest`.
   - Commit: `git commit -m "[CAN-XXX] feat: <description>"`.
   - Push: `git push -u origin feat/<issue-id>-<description>`.
   - Mark in-review: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --mark-in-review <issue-id>`.
   - Provide PR link with `Closes CAN-XXX` and designated triangular reviewer:
     * Benjamin's PRs -> Assign Samir (@samiroibrahim)
     * Samir's PRs -> Assign Yassir (@yassir-tagelsir-khougali)
     * Yassir's PRs -> Assign Benjamin (@neobenjax)
3. After PR merge:
   - Mark task done in TASKS.md & Linear: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --mark-done <issue-id>`.
   - Purge feature branch: `git checkout main && git pull origin main && git branch -d <branch> && git push origin --delete <branch>`.

## ACCOUNT SETUP & AUTOMATION COMMANDS
- SSH Commit Signing: See `docs/DEVELOPER_SETUP_AND_AUTOMATION_GUIDE.md`. Assist developer with `git config --global gpg.format ssh` and `commit.gpgsign true`.
- Task Tracking CLI:
  * Check overall status: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --status`
  * Check member tasks: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --owner <Name>`
  * Sync with Linear cloud: `python scripts/sync_tasks.py --status --sync-linear`

## 2026 STANDARDS
- Python 3.12+ with `uv` package manager. Run `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run pytest`.
- FastMCP 2.0 (Anthropic MCP SDK) + LangGraph 0.2+ + DuckDB 1.2+ Apache Arrow zero-copy memory.
- Design: Follow Custom Active Theme design tokens and Google Chrome's modern-web-guidance.
- Demos: Use `frontend-slides` (https://github.com/zarazhangrui/frontend-slides) for weekly demo presentations.

